  "description": "AGSC-11-20: a node whose `agsc-visibility` is `restricted` MUST carry exactly one `https://w3id.org/agentic-system-core/rel#access` link, whose target names where a reader obtains credentials, and it asserts conformance for its unauthenticated view at Level 0; a discovery checker (AGSC-09-93) asks for that link at every Level. Derivation, case by case. Each document is the Level-0 view of one restricted node at https://example.org: the anchor's `describedby` link carries the two attributes AGSC-11-20 keeps on a restricted node (`agsc-generated-at`, `agsc-spec-version`) and `agsc-visibility: [\"restricted\"]`, with no digest and none of the four content facts; the `alternate` link names /llms.txt and the `license` link the legal page. The documents differ only in the access link. (1) restricted-without-access-link carries none: the required link is missing, so the checker reports exactly one error, AGSC-E202, as for any other missing required member. (2) restricted-with-two-access-links carries two, to /access/ and /access/other/: the rule says exactly one, so the declaration disagrees with the rule, and the checker reports exactly one error, AGSC-E210, once for the relation and not once per link. (3) restricted-with-one-access-link carries one, to /access/, with `agsc-access: [\"credential\"]`: it is valid, with no finding. Nothing else in any document is a fault, so each list of findings is complete.",
